import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Deployment — Acme Docs">
  <p><a href="/docs">Documentation</a> / Guides / Deployment</p>
  <h1>Two deploys. One address.</h1>
  <ol>
    <li>Create separate docs and marketing projects on Vercel.</li>
    <li>Leave each Vercel project's Root Directory empty. The workflow runs inside <code>apps/docs</code> or <code>apps/marketing</code>, builds with that app's <code>vercel.json</code>, and uploads its generated artifacts.</li>
    <li>Add the four Vercel repository secrets listed in the README to GitHub Actions.</li>
    <li>Push to <code>main</code>. The workflow deploys docs, fills marketing's <code>vercel.json</code> with that deployment URL, then deploys marketing.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Pull-request previews</h2>
  <p>Open a pull request targeting <code>main</code> from a branch in this repository to deploy a preview of both apps. New commits update the preview. Find its URL in the GitHub environment named <code>preview-pr-N</code> or the Actions run summary. The marketing preview proxies to the docs preview from the same run.</p>
  <h2>How routing works</h2>
  <p>Marketing serves its own Astro pages. Requests to <code>/docs</code> and <code>/docs/*</code> are proxied to the docs project. The marketing domain stays in the address bar.</p>
  <p>Astro-generated docs assets live under <code>/docs/_astro</code>, so they travel through the same proxy.</p>
  <h2>URLs without trailing slashes</h2>
  <p>Both apps use <code>trailingSlash: "never"</code> and <code>build.format: "file"</code>. Use links such as <code>/about</code> and <code>/docs/getting-started</code>.</p>
  <p>The repository README contains platform settings, CLI instructions, and deployment checks.</p>
</Layout>
